# Stage 6 Traundl chain (D-077, D-085; game-design.md Stage 6 section 5):
# the solver route to frame 2560 (swimming past the lantern pontoon), then
# by hand: float until Traundl A comes back to its spawn end above her,
# jump out onto it (press 2746), ride A to its far end, hop to the border
# raft (press 2866). Gelse #2 (col 154, row 6) starts hunting at 2870 and
# comes down on her on the raft (standing still it would reach her at
# 2952, 64 frames before B docks at ~3016): a standing full jump (press
# 2925) stomps it. Hop onto Traundl B as it docks (press 3007), ride B to
# its far end, hop onto C (press 3141), ride C to its far-end berth
# (~3273), jump up onto the Zaunerstollen perch (press 3273). Gelse #3
# (col 171, row 6, hunting from 3233) comes up to her on the perch; a
# standing full jump stomps it (press 3332). Then under the Z-box (col 175,
# row 4), bump it; the Zaunerstollen rolls right, turns at the bollard
# (177) and comes back to her: 1-up.
# Hand-measured press windows (only that press shifted, the rest
# unchanged; counted = she ends dry on the target / the Gelse is stomped):
# jump-out onto A 52 frames (2733-2784), A -> raft 41 (2857-2897), Gelse
# #2 stomp >= 41 (2905-2945, every shift tried), raft -> B 45 (2987-3031),
# B -> C 27 (3128-3154), C -> perch >= 39 (3265-3303, every shift tried),
# Gelse #3 stomp >= 23 (3321-3343, every shift tried).
# Gelse #3 never touches her during the C ride (3176-3273): standing on C
# at its far end she would first be reached at 3306, as C leaves the berth.
